  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#htmlconstructor says:\r\n\r\n> all HTML elements have special constructor behavior\r\n\r\nbut there are various HTML element interfaces that do not have [HTMLConstructor] extended attributes.  Specifically, these are:\r\n\r\n* HTMLAppletElement\r\n* HTMLUnknownElement\r\n* HTMLFrameElement\r\n* HTMLFrameSetElement\r\n* HTMLHeadElement\r\n\r\nSee also https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1274159#c37\r\n\r\nFor some of these (e.g. HTMLUnknownElement) there might be specific reasons the extended attribute wasn't added, though in that case it might be good to have an IDL comment or spec note about those reasons.  But for  the others, it's not at all clear to me why it wasn't added...\r\n\r\n@domenic @annevk ",
